This position ensures quality assurance and aligned measurement approaches across a range of program strategies and project plans. The Program Quality and Design Coordinator (PQDC) will facilitate and support program staff in the design of new projects aligned to GSD standards and partners' plans. Designs will address sustainability and measurement outcomes aligned to the GSD Measurement Framework. Over time, the position will help ensure GSD's impact measurement approaches are appropriately embedded in program strategies and project plans and contribute to system change.

The PQDC will lead capacity strengthening of GSD staff in project design, quality assurance, and efficient design facilitation with partners. Planning support will include working with the Partnerships' team and external partners to develop evidence-based, multi-year, country plans as well as helping GSD develop multi-year regional plans.
The role will also support the scale up and implementation of the Disaster Preparedness and Response Readiness Index (DPR2I) with partner countries across the Caribbean and Central America. The role will also support the Program Quality Evaluator in the design and implementation of project and program evaluations.

**ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS:**

1. Lead the process to facilitate and co-facilitate the design of preparedness projects, with GSD program staff (i.e. technical subject matter experts, program and project managers, partnership focal points) and partners, in the Caribbean and Central America aligned to program strategies and in accordance with organizational expectations. This includes building Monitoring, Evaluation, and Learning (MEL) systems, theories of change, and results frameworks from scratch in a participatory manner with internal and external stakeholders;
