Support the development and roll-out of a multi-year planning process with the Partnerships' team and external partners, ensuring alignment with the GSD Measurement Framework including core approaches, such as the Disaster Preparedness and Response Readiness Index (DPR2I);
3. Build capacity of GSD staff in external program quality and design with a specific focus on quality and sustainability in programs (i.e. Response Coordination, Mental Health & Psychosocial Support, Maritime Access, Information Management, and Water interoperability);
4. Lead the design and execution of a clear sustainability framework, tailored to GSD's program areas and innovation priorities;
5. Support the Portfolios team in the development and use of quality assurance tools in support of monitoring and project oversight;
6. Develop and deliver capacity-building sessions aligned to the Portfolio team's needs in project planning and implementation. This will include, but is not limited to, best practices in project design and project management and sustainability management needed to help GSD achieve its ambition;
7. Design and facilitate biannual programs, project strategy results and learning sessions, ensuring alignment with the Program Section leadership expectations;
8. Lead or support the scalability and application of the DPR2I, helping to ensure its results inform GSD's work across preparedness, response and innovation;
9. Support the Director in the adaptation and implementation of GSD Measurement Framework ensuring alignment across strategy, sub-strategies, programs and projects;
10. Support the Program Quality Evaluator in the design, execution, and management of preparedness evaluations and response after action reviews in accordance with the learning agenda;
11. Promote good stewardship of financial and other resources to achieve maximum benefit to those impacted by disaster or at risk of impact;
12. Promote and embody GSD's core values of accountability, humility, and integrity across all areas of responsibility;
13. Foster a culture of excellence and equity, prioritizing inclusion and learning in all aspects of program quality and performance measurement; and
14. Perform other duties as assigned.

**QUALIFICATIONS:**

**Required Experience:**

