Background

Being a development entity, UNDP has a central role in terms of development knowledge sharing, building and strengthening national and state level capacities. UNDP continues to ensure that the achievement of the global Agenda 2030 and its 17 Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) remain at the forefront in terms of the national and state level development agenda. UNDP’s commitment continues to focus on inclusivity and sustainability, to empower lives and to build a resilient nation and resilient communities.

Under the leadership and direct supervision of the Resident Representative, the Communications and Partnerships Specialist will work with the Senior Management to spearhead the Country Office (CO) overall efforts to support the National Development Strategy (NDS), accelerate the implementation of the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), the UN Sustainable Development Framework (UNSCDF) and UNDP’s Country Program Document (CPD) for South Sudan.

